# Own-words summaries of non-SRD spells (G–R).
NOTES = {
"Swift Courier": ("1 action", "10 feet", "V, S, M (25 gold pieces, consumed)", "10 minutes",
  "You summon a small air elemental beside a chest that opens for the duration. Put whatever fits inside, name a creature you've met on this plane, and when the spell ends the elemental carries the chest's contents straight to that creature (or back, if it can't be found).", "The duration rises with more mana: 1 hour at 5th, 8 hours at 6th, 24 hours at 7th level."),
"Tower of Walls": ("10 minutes", "30 feet", "V, S, M (a fragment of stone, wood or other building material)", "24 hours",
  "You conjure a two-story tower of stone, wood or similar material on open ground. Each floor is a 10-foot square room with a door, stairs and a window. It has furnishings and is lit. Creatures inside can see out but the outside is opaque. It vanishes when the spell ends.", "One more story for each level above 3rd."),
"Gate Seal": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a broken portal key, consumed)", "24 hours",
  "You seal a 30-foot cube against planar travel. No portal or gate in it can be used, and nothing can teleport or plane shift in or out of it.", "Cast with the 60 mana of a 6th-level spell or more, the seal lasts until dispelled."),
"Gift of Alacrity": ("1 minute", "Touch", "V, S", "8 hours",
  "You touch a willing creature and give it a feel for the flow of time. For the duration it adds 1d8 to its initiative rolls.", ""),
"Gift of Gab": ("1 reaction, when you speak", "Self", "V, S, M (2 gold pieces, consumed)", "Instantaneous",
  "When you say something you regret, you take it back: every creature within 15 feet that heard what you said in the last 6 seconds forgets it, and you can say something else in its place. They remember only the new version.", ""),
"Grasping Vine": ("1 bonus action", "30 feet", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A vine sprouts from the ground at a point you can see. When you cast it, and as a bonus action on later turns, the vine lashes at a creature within 30 feet of it: a Dexterity save or be pulled 20 feet toward the vine.", ""),
"Grave Ground": None,
"Gravity Fissure": ("1 action", "Self (100-foot line)", "V, S, M (a fistful of iron filings)", "Instantaneous",
  "You open a 100-foot line, 5 feet wide, of crushing gravity. Each creature in it makes a Constitution save, taking 8d8 force damage on a failure or half on a success. Each creature within 10 feet of the line but not in it makes the save too or is pulled toward the line.", "Damage rises by 1d8 for each level above 6th."),
"Gravity Sinkhole": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S, M (a black marble)", "Instantaneous",
  "A 20-foot-radius sphere of crushing force forms at a point. Each creature in it makes a Constitution save, taking 5d10 force damage on a failure or half on a success, and those that fail are pulled toward the center.", "Damage rises by 1d10 for each level above 4th."),
"Green-Flame Blade": ("1 action", "Self (5-foot radius)", "S, M (a melee weapon)", "Instantaneous",
  "Make a melee weapon attack as part of the spell. On a hit, the target suffers the weapon's normal effects, and green fire leaps to a second creature within 5 feet of it, dealing fire damage equal to your spellcasting modifier. The damage grows at 5th, 11th and 17th level (extra fire on the first target and more on the leap).", ""),
"Guardian of Nature": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A nature spirit transforms you. Primal Beast: +10 speed, darkvision 120, advantage on Strength attacks, and 1d6 extra force damage on melee weapon hits. Great Tree: 10 temporary hit points, advantage on Constitution saves and on Dexterity and Wisdom attacks, and the ground near you becomes difficult terrain for your enemies.", ""),
"Gust": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V, S", "Instantaneous",
  "You seize the air: push a Medium or smaller creature 5 feet (Strength save), push an object up to 5 pounds 10 feet, or make a harmless sensory effect like rustling leaves or slamming shutters.", ""),
"Hail of Thorns": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "The next time you hit with a ranged weapon attack before the spell ends, your ammunition explodes into thorns. The target and each creature within 5 feet of it make a Dexterity save, taking 1d10 piercing damage on a failure or half on a success.", "Damage rises by 1d10 for each level above 1st."),
"Healing Spirit": ("1 bonus action", "60 feet", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A nature spirit fills a 5-foot cube. When you or a creature you can see moves into it for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, you can have it heal that creature for 1d6. It can heal a number of times equal to 1 + your spellcasting modifier. You can move it 30 feet as a bonus action.", "Healing rises by 1d6 for each level above 2nd."),
"Hindsight": None,
"Holy Star of Mystra": None,
"Holy Weapon": ("1 bonus action", "Touch", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "A weapon you touch glows with holy light (bright light in 30 feet). Attacks with it deal an extra 2d8 radiant damage. As a bonus action, the wielder can end the spell in a burst: each creature of their choice within 30 feet makes a Constitution save, taking 4d8 radiant damage and being blinded for a minute on a failure, or half damage only on a success.", ""),
"Homunculus Servant": None,
"Hunger of Hadar": ("1 action", "150 feet", "V, S, M (a pickled octopus tentacle)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You open a gateway to the dark between the stars: a 20-foot-radius sphere of blackness and bitter cold. Nothing can see inside it, and it is difficult terrain. A creature starting its turn there takes 2d6 cold damage; one ending its turn there makes a Dexterity save or takes 2d6 acid damage as unseen things lick at it.", ""),
"Illusory Dragon": ("1 action", "120 feet", "S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A Huge shadowy dragon appears. When it appears, each creature you choose that can see it makes a Wisdom save or is frightened for a minute. As a bonus action you can move it 60 feet and have it breathe a 60-foot cone: Intelligence save, 7d6 damage of a type you choose (acid, cold, fire, lightning, necrotic or poison), half on a success. It can't be harmed and an Investigation check reveals it as an illusion.", ""),
"Immolation": ("1 action", "90 feet", "V", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "Flames wreathe a creature you can see. It makes a Dexterity save, taking 8d6 fire damage on a failure or half on a success. On a failure it keeps burning, taking 4d6 fire at the end of each of its turns and saving again to end it. It sheds light and can be put out by water. A creature killed by it turns to ash.", ""),
"Immovable Object": ("1 action", "Touch", "V, S, M (gold dust worth 25 gp, consumed)", "1 hour",
  "You fix an object of 10 pounds or less in place. It can't move unless a creature succeeds on a Strength check against your DC (and you can name creatures who can move it freely). It can hold up to 4,000 pounds.", "At 4th or 5th level: the Strength DC to move it rises by 5, it holds 8,000 pounds, and it lasts 24 hours. At 6th or higher: DC +10, 20,000 pounds, and it lasts until dispelled."),
"Incite Greed": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V, S, M (a gem worth at least 50 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You hold up the gem and its glitter calls to others. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet that can see you makes a Wisdom save or is charmed: it must move toward you on its turn and can't take actions other than moving or gawking until it's within 5 feet, and it can't move away.", ""),
"Infernal Calling": ("1 minute", "90 feet", "V, S, M (a ruby worth 999 gp)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "You call a devil of challenge rating 6 or lower from the Nine Hells. It isn't friendly to you; it does what you say only if it wants to, and you can bargain with it. If you know its true name or hold its talisman, it's easier to control. When the spell ends it goes home. (In Avarenth, devils are the DM's to place; this may reach your patron's enemies.)", "The devil's challenge rating rises by 1 for each level above 5th."),
"Infestation": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V, S, M (a living flea)", "Instantaneous",
  "A cloud of mites, fleas and lice covers a creature. It makes a Constitution save or takes 1d6 poison damage and moves 5 feet in a random direction (if it can). Damage grows to 2d6 at 5th level, 3d6 at 11th and 4d6 at 17th.", ""),
"Inflict Doubt": None,
"Intellect Fortress": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "A shimmering mental barrier guards one creature. It has resistance to psychic damage and advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves.", "One more creature for each level above 3rd, all within 30 feet of each other."),
"Investiture of Flame": ("1 action", "Self", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "Flames race across your body. You shed light, are immune to fire, resist cold, and creatures that move within 5 feet of you or hit you in melee take 1d10 fire damage. As an action, you can blast a 15-foot line of fire: Dexterity save, 4d8 fire, half on a success.", ""),
"Investiture of Ice": ("1 action", "Self", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "Ice rimes your body. You are immune to cold, resist fire, move across ice easily, and the ground within 10 feet of you is difficult terrain for others. As an action, you can blast a 15-foot cone of freezing wind: Constitution save, 4d6 cold and slowed, half and no slow on a success.", ""),
"Investiture of Stone": ("1 action", "Self", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "Rocky plates cover your body. You resist nonmagical bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage. As an action, you can make the ground in a 15-foot radius shake: each other creature there makes a Dexterity save or falls prone. You can move through stone and earth as if it were difficult terrain.", ""),
"Investiture of Wind": ("1 action", "Self", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "Wind whirls around you. Ranged weapon attacks against you have disadvantage, and you gain a flying speed of 60 feet. As an action, you can create a 15-foot cube of swirling wind within 60 feet: Constitution save, 2d10 bludgeoning, half on a success, and a Large or smaller creature that fails is pushed 10 feet.", ""),
"Invulnerability": ("1 action", "Self", "V, S, M (a small piece of adamantine worth 500 gp, consumed)", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "You are immune to all damage until the spell ends.", ""),
"Iron Body": None,
"Storm of Radiance": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S, M (a pinch of phosphorus)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "Radiant hail and thunder fill a 10-foot-radius, 40-foot-high cylinder. Inside, creatures are blinded and deafened, and can't cast spells with verbal components. A creature that enters it for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there makes a Constitution save, taking 2d10 radiant and 2d10 thunder damage on a failure or half on a success.", "Each damage type rises by 1d10 for each level above 5th."),
"Glowing Coin": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a coin)", "1 minute",
  "You throw a coin and it starts glowing and making noise. Each creature of your choice within 60 feet that can see it makes a Wisdom save or is distracted: it has disadvantage on Perception checks and initiative rolls until the spell ends. Disturbing the coin ends the spell.", ""),
"Arcane Darts": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S", "Instantaneous",
  "Three glowing darts fly at creatures you choose. Unlike Magic Missile, each needs a ranged spell attack, dealing 2d4 force on a hit. On a natural 1 they all miss and hit you for 1 damage each; on a natural 20 each deals 5d4.", "One more dart for each level above 1st."),
"Kinetic Jaunt": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You magically empower your movement. Your walking speed rises by 10 feet, moving doesn't provoke opportunity attacks, and you can move through other creatures' spaces (as difficult terrain). You can't end your turn in another creature's space.", ""),
"Silver Lance": None,
"Life Transference": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V, S", "Instantaneous",
  "You sacrifice your own life to mend another. You take 4d8 necrotic damage, which can't be reduced, and a creature you can see heals twice that much.", "Damage (and healing) rise by 1d8 for each level above 3rd."),
"Lightning Arrow": ("1 bonus action", "Self", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "The next time you make a ranged weapon attack, your ammunition becomes a bolt of lightning. Make the attack as normal: the target takes 4d8 lightning damage on a hit or half on a miss, instead of the weapon's damage. Then each creature within 10 feet of the target makes a Dexterity save, taking 2d8 lightning damage, half on a success.", "Both damages rise by 1d8 for each level above 3rd."),
"Lightning Lure": ("1 action", "Self (15-foot radius)", "V", "Instantaneous",
  "A lash of lightning strikes a creature within 15 feet. It makes a Strength save or is pulled up to 10 feet toward you, then takes 1d8 lightning damage if it's within 5 feet of you. Damage grows to 2d8 at 5th level, 3d8 at 11th and 4d8 at 17th.", ""),
"Lightning Ring": None,
"Linked Glyphs": ("1 hour", "Touch", "V, S, M (powdered diamond worth 200 gp, consumed)", "Until dispelled or triggered",
  "You draw two linked glyphs, which must be on the same plane. When the first is triggered, the second unleashes its stored spell or effect where it is, so a trap on one side of a dungeon can go off on the other. Works like Glyph of Warding.", ""),
"Maddening Darkness": ("1 action", "150 feet", "V, M (a drop of pitch mixed with a drop of mercury)", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "Magical darkness fills a 60-foot-radius sphere. Not even darkvision sees through it; nonmagical light can't light it. Shrieks and laughter fill it. A creature starting its turn there makes a Wisdom save, taking 8d8 psychic damage on a failure or half on a success.", ""),
"Maelstrom": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S, M (paper or leaf in the shape of a funnel)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A swirling 30-foot-radius, 5-foot-deep pool of water appears on the ground. It's difficult terrain, and a creature starting its turn there makes a Strength save or takes 6d6 bludgeoning damage and is pulled 10 feet toward the center.", ""),
"Magic Stone": ("1 bonus action", "Touch", "V, S", "1 minute",
  "You touch up to three pebbles and fill them with magic. A creature can throw one or sling it, making a ranged spell attack with your spellcasting modifier for 1d6 + that modifier bludgeoning damage.", ""),
"Magnify Gravity": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a small iron ball)", "1 round",
  "Gravity in a 10-foot-radius sphere grows heavy. Each creature there makes a Constitution save, taking 2d8 force damage on a failure (or half on a success), and on a failure its speed is halved until the end of its next turn. Objects there get harder to lift.", "Damage rises by 1d8 for each level above 1st."),
"Mass Polymorph": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V, S, M (a caterpillar cocoon)", "Concentration, up to 1 hour",
  "Like Polymorph, but up to ten creatures. Each unwilling creature makes a Wisdom save. Each one you change becomes a beast of challenge rating no higher than its own (or half its level), keeping its hit points as a buffer.", ""),
"Earthen Grasp": ("1 action", "30 feet", "V, S, M (a miniature hand sculpted from clay)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "A Medium hand of compacted earth rises in a 5-foot square. When it appears, and as an action on later turns, it reaches for a creature within 5 feet of it: a Strength save or take 2d6 bludgeoning damage and be restrained. You can crush a restrained creature for 2d6 as an action, or move the hand 30 feet.", ""),
"Minute Meteors": ("1 action", "Self", "V, S, M (niter, sulfur and pine tar formed into a bead)", "Concentration, up to 10 minutes",
  "Six tiny meteors orbit you. As a bonus action you can send one or two at points within 120 feet; each explodes, and each creature within 5 feet makes a Dexterity save, taking 2d6 fire damage on a failure or half on a success.", "Two more meteors for each level above 3rd."),
"Mental Prison": ("1 action", "60 feet", "S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You trap a creature in an illusion it can't escape. It takes 5d10 psychic damage on a failed Intelligence save (half on a success, and the spell ends). On a failure it sees itself surrounded by danger: if it moves out, or reaches through the illusion, it takes 10d10 psychic damage and the spell ends.", ""),
"Mighty Fortress": ("1 minute", "1 mile", "V, S, M (a diamond worth 500 gp, consumed)", "Instantaneous",
  "A stone fortress rises from the ground: a 120-foot-square keep with four towers, walls, a courtyard and furnished rooms. A hundred spectral servants attend it. It lasts 7 days, then crumbles; cast it in the same place every 7 days for a year and it's permanent.", ""),
"Mind Splinter": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V", "1 round",
  "You drive a spike of psychic energy into a creature. It makes an Intelligence save or takes 1d6 psychic damage and subtracts 1d4 from the next save it makes before the end of your next turn. Damage grows to 2d6 at 5th level, 3d6 at 11th and 4d6 at 17th.", ""),
"Mold Earth": ("1 action", "30 feet", "S", "Instantaneous or 1 hour",
  "You shape dirt or sand in a 5-foot cube: dig it out and drop it within 5 feet, carve shapes or colors into it for an hour, or turn it into difficult terrain (or back) for an hour.", ""),
"Moment of Prescience": None,
"Deep Study": None,
"Motivational Speech": ("1 minute", "60 feet", "V", "1 hour",
  "Up to five creatures who listen to your speech gain 5 temporary hit points and advantage on Wisdom saves for the duration. When one is hit by an attack, it has advantage on the next attack roll it makes. When a creature loses all its temporary hit points, the spell ends for it.", "Temporary hit points rise by 5 for each level above 3rd."),
"Mischief Cascade": ("1 action", "60 feet", "S, M (a piece of crust from an apple pie)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "Fey mischief fills a 20-foot cube. At the start of each of your turns, roll a d4: charmed (Wisdom save or charmed by you), blinded (Wisdom save or blinded), dazzled (difficult terrain and disadvantage on concentration), or spraying (sweet-smelling sprite dust that makes creatures fall prone on a Dex save).", ""),
"Negative Energy Flood": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, M (a broken bone and a square of black silk)", "Instantaneous",
  "You send dark energy at a creature you can see. If it's undead, it gains 5d12 temporary hit points. Otherwise it makes a Constitution save, taking 5d12 necrotic damage on a failure or half on a success; if that kills it, it rises as a zombie at the start of your next turn and attacks the nearest creature.", ""),
"Power Word Fortify": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V", "Instantaneous",
  "You speak a word of strength and share out 120 temporary hit points as you choose among up to six creatures you can see.", ""),
"Power Word Pain": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V", "Instantaneous",
  "A word of power wracks a creature with 100 hit points or fewer. Its speed drops to 10 feet, it has disadvantage on attacks, checks and saves (except Constitution), and to cast a spell it must pass a Constitution save. It repeats a Constitution save at the end of each of its turns. Creatures immune to charm aren't affected.", ""),
"Primal Savagery": ("1 action", "Self", "S", "Instantaneous",
  "Your teeth or nails grow sharp. Make a melee spell attack against a creature within 5 feet, dealing 1d10 acid damage on a hit. Damage grows to 2d10 at 5th level, 3d10 at 11th and 4d10 at 17th.", ""),
"Primordial Ward": ("1 action", "Self", "V, S", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You have resistance to acid, cold, fire, lightning and thunder damage. When you take damage of one of those types, you can use your reaction to gain immunity to it instead, ending the spell at the end of your next turn.", ""),
"Psychic Scream": ("1 action", "90 feet", "S", "Instantaneous",
  "You unleash the power of your mind on up to ten creatures with Intelligence 3 or higher. Each makes an Intelligence save, taking 14d6 psychic damage and being stunned on a failure, or half and no stun on a success. A creature killed by it has its head explode. Stunned creatures repeat the save each turn.", ""),
"Pulse Wave": ("1 action", "Self (30-foot cone)", "V, S", "Instantaneous",
  "A wave of force rolls out in a 30-foot cone. Each creature there makes a Constitution save, taking 6d6 force damage on a failure or half on a success. On a failure you can pull or push it up to 15 feet.", "Damage rises by 1d6, and the push by 5 feet, for each level above 3rd."),
"Pyrotechnics": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S", "Instantaneous",
  "Pick a nonmagical flame you can see. It goes out, and becomes either fireworks (each creature within 10 feet makes a Constitution save or is blinded until the end of your next turn) or thick smoke (a 20-foot cloud that blocks sight for a minute).", ""),
"Psychic Lance": ("1 action", "120 feet", "V", "Instantaneous",
  "A shimmering lance of psychic power leaps at a creature you can see, or one you name (if it's within range, even behind cover). It makes an Intelligence save, taking 7d6 psychic damage and becoming incapacitated until your next turn on a failure, or half damage only on a success.", "Damage rises by 1d6 for each level above 4th."),
"Ravenous Void": ("1 action", "1,000 feet", "V, S, M (a small, nine-pointed star made of iron)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You create a 20-foot-radius sphere of destructive gravity. It's difficult terrain, and creatures within 100 feet of it are pulled 20 feet toward it each turn (Strength save). A creature that starts its turn inside is restrained, takes 5d10 force damage and has its items pulled away; one reduced to 0 hit points is torn to nothing.", ""),
"Reality Break": ("1 action", "60 feet", "V, S, M (a crystal prism)", "Concentration, up to 1 minute",
  "You shatter a creature's grip on reality. It makes a Wisdom save or can't take reactions, and at the start of each of its turns it rolls a d10: 1–2, visions of the void stun it until its turn ends and it takes 6d12 psychic damage; 3–5, a rift tears at it (Dexterity save or 8d12 force); 6–8, it's flung up to 30 feet through a wormhole, taking 10d12 force and falling prone; 9–10, the cold between worlds takes 10d12 cold damage and blinds it until its turn ends. It makes a Wisdom save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on a success.", ""),
"Reweave Fate": None,
"Binding Ice": ("1 action", "Self (30-foot cone)", "S, M (a vial of meltwater)", "Instantaneous",
  "A burst of cold erupts from you in a 30-foot cone. Each creature there makes a Constitution save, taking 3d8 cold damage on a failure or half on a success. Those that fail are encased in ice: their speed is 0 until they or someone else breaks the ice (an action, AC 10, 15 hit points).", "Damage rises by 1d8 for each level above 2nd."),
}
